		ctx = templ.ClearChildren(ctx)
		templ_7745c5c3_Err = templruntime.WriteString(templ_7745c5c3_Buffer, 12, "<article id=\"glass\"><p>Glass is one of the most recyclable materials in the world, and recycling it can significantly reduce waste and conserve resources.  Recycling glass helps cut down the need for raw materials like sand, reduces energy consumption, and keeps non-biodegradable waste out of landfills. </p><p>Not all glass is recyclable. Items like glass bottles, jars, clear glass and colored glass (green and brown) are typically accepted at recycling centers. However, other types of glass, such as window panes, mirrors, ceramics, or lightbulbs, may not be recyclable because they contain additives or are treated differently during production. Before recycling, ensure that the glass items you have are the correct type. </p><p>Before you recycle glass, it’s very important to clean it thoroughly. This means removing any leftover food, liquids, or labels.  Contaminated glass can affect the recycling process, so rinse jars and bottles with water before placing them in the recycling bin. For instance, if you’re recycling a tomato sauce jar, rinse it out to remove leftover sauce. Don’t worry about removing every bit of glue from the label; the recycling facilities handle that.</p><p>In Nigeria, dedicated recycling facilities or drop-off points are important for proper waste management. A company like Bel Tech makes it easier by providing designated collection points where you can drop off your recyclable materials, including glass. Check if your community has a recycling center nearby or if programs like Bel Tech operate in your area. With Bel Tech’s app, you can even track collection points and earn rewards for recycling.</p><p>If you’re recycling broken glass, handle it with caution to avoid injury. Wrap sharp edges in newspaper or place them in a sturdy container before transporting them to the recycling center. Important Tip: Never throw broken glass directly into your recycling bin without protecting it, as it can harm waste handlers.</p><p>One of the unique ways Bel Tech promotes recycling in Nigeria is by offering incentives. By dropping off your recyclable glass at designated Bel Tech collection points, you can earn tokens or rewards that can be redeemed for goods or services. This encourages proper waste management while benefiting the environment and the recycler.</p><p>Recycling glass is an easy and impactful way to reduce waste and promote sustainability in your community.  You can contribute to a cleaner environment and even earn rewards with platforms like Bel Tech by following these steps; cleaning, sorting, and dropping off glass at the right centers.</p></article>")
